pageType: table
background:
  type: solid
  color: "$paper"
notes: >-
  Read the table left to right: for every deliverable in the plan, one person
  owns it. Owners decide; everyone else gives input. If two names appear next
  to one deliverable, the kickoff is not finished — pick one. The AI assistant
  is a tool, not a decision-maker: it drafts, summarizes, and tracks so the
  humans can focus on the judgment calls. The check: point at any line in the
  plan and the owner raises their hand.
elements:
  - elementId: t
    elementType: text
    bounds: [46, 36, 840, 46]
    content:
      style: "$title"
      wrap: false
      text: "Every deliverable has an owner"
  - elementId: tb
    elementType: table
    bounds: [46, 168, 868, 312]
    columnWidths: [0.22, 0.42, 0.36]
    rows:
      - - text: "Role"
        - text: "Owns the decision"
        - text: "Brings to the kickoff"
      - - text: "Facilitator"
        - text: "The agenda and the output"
        - text: "A one-page plan, captured live"
      - - text: "Product Owner"
        - text: "What we build — and what we don't"
        - text: "Problem statement + success metric"
      - - text: "Engineering Lead"
        - text: "How it's built, and how long"
        - text: "Effort estimates + risks"
      - - text: "Design Lead"
        - text: "What users experience"
        - text: "Flows, prototypes, open questions"
      - - text: "AI assistant"
        - text: "Drafting, summarizing, tracking"
        - text: "Raw inputs + the follow-up list"
      - - text: "Everyone"
        - text: "Their own workstream"
        - text: "Commitment to dates, honest status"
